-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- 0039_names_rule_9 — the name rule, ninth version (S-03, phase 1b). 0039_names_rule_8.sql is applied and never edited; this file
-- runs right after it (the same number: 0040–0069 belong to other branches) and replaces the rule's generated functions.
--   Found after 0039_names_rule_8 (verifier round 8, v-spoof8): the skeleton joined أ / آ with ا (and ة / ه, ى / ي / ئ) but not
--   إ with ا nor ؤ with و. Egyptians usually type a name without its hamza, so a look-alike «ابراهيم حسن» registered with the real
--   «إبراهيم حسن»'s company and city was the ONLY option for the sender who typed «ابراهيم حسن» — no ⚠️, and the message reached the
--   look-alike (EN / AR, 1440 / 390). The same for إسلام، إيمان، فؤاد، مؤمن، لؤي.
--   THE FIX (decision ض, under the owner's over-merge principle ق — close the TYPING family as a whole, not letter by letter):
--   • the skeleton (person_name_key, profiles.name_key) folds every way a name is TYPED in its own script: every mark is dropped
--     (إ أ آ → ا, ؤ → و, ئ → ي, é → e, й → и, ά → α), a letter written with a hamza / madda / wasla is its letter (ٱ → ا — from
--     ArabicShaping.txt), a hamza on no letter (ء) is dropped, a Latin / Greek / Cyrillic letter people type plainly is its plain
--     letter(s) (ø → o, đ → d, ł → l, æ → ae, ß → ss, þ → th — the Unicode root collation), every allowed punctuation mark is dropped
--     (as spaces and the apostrophe were), and a title at the start (Dr., د., Eng., م., Prof., Ph. … — the greeting's own list) is
--     dropped: «Dr. Ahmed Ali» = «Ahmed Ali»;
--   • a new SEARCH-ONLY key, profiles.name_sound (person_name_sound — kept by the same trigger, trigram-indexed): the consonants of a
--     name as it is typed in Latin letters (Mohamed / Mohammed / Muhammad, Abdel / Abd El / Abdul, Youssef / Yusuf, Hussein /
--     Hussain…), Arabic letters in the same classes. It only ADDS members to what the ✎ picker offers — never a twin, never a resolve;
--   • ى / ں are refused only where they join the next letter (Joining_Type D / R, ArabicShaping.txt): «هانىء», «شاطىء» are allowed;
--     a space on one side of a hyphen is refused ('dash', the message offers the fix: «Abdel-Rahman», «Ahmed Ali (MBA)») instead of
--     being joined silently; a zero-width space is removed where it draws nothing and a space only where it breaks an Arabic join;
--     the 'word' refusal quotes what was typed («ʿ»).
--   The rule is generated, identical in the live app, by tools/names/name_rule.mjs (Unicode 16.0.0 data in tools/names/).
--   EXISTING NAMES: NOTHING IS RENAMED; a name the new rule refuses is FLAGGED (name_needs_fix), every row is keyed again and gets its
--   sound key. Counts: RAISE NOTICE (names now twins, names a one-sided hyphen flags, names ى before ء no longer flags).
-- Every function and table keeps or gets its GRANT/REVOKE (0026). Safe to run twice.
-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

